{
  "task": {
    "id": "Prob133_2014_q3fsm",
    "spec": "\r\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\r\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\r\nspecified.\r\n\r\n - input  clk\r\n - input  reset\r\n - input  s\r\n - input  w\r\n - output z\r\n\r\nThe module should implement a finite state machine with inputs s and w.\r\nAssume that the FSM begins in a reset state called A, as depicted below.\r\nThe FSM remains in state A as long as s = 0, and it moves to state B when\r\ns = 1. Once in state B the FSM examines the value of the input w in the\r\nnext three clock cycles. If w = 1 in exactly two of these clock cycles,\r\nthen the FSM has to set an output z to 1 in the following clock cycle.\r\nOtherwise z has to be 0. The FSM continues checking w for the next three\r\nclock cycles, and so on. Use as few states as possible. Note that the s\r\ninput is used only in state A, so you need to consider just the w input.\r\nAssume reset is active high synchronous. Assume all sequential logic is\r\ntriggered on the positive edge of the clock.\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "clk",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "reset",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "s",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "w",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "z",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."
  },
  "sample_id": "6b79bab3-7fdb-4428-a0a6-8f618e0cb0cc",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "e35214ea-26bd-4e15-af49-521f42abf9dd",
    "source_sha256": "2c90b7a83544ef28990a5e6bfa923389e47335c11faade785a42ec1cb7d4834b",
    "source": "module TopModule (\n    input  clk,\n    input  reset,\n    input  s,\n    input  w,\n    output z\n);\n\n    // State encoding:\n    // A  : reset/idle state (only place where s is examined)\n    // B  : first w sample of a 3-cycle group\n    // C0 : after one sample, count = 0\n    // C1 : after one sample, count = 1\n    // D0 : after two samples, count = 0\n    // D1 : after two samples, count = 1\n    // D2 : after two samples, count = 2\n    // E0 : output cycle, previous group did not have exactly two ones\n    // E1 : output cycle, previous group had exactly two ones\n    localparam A  = 4'd0;\n    localparam B  = 4'd1;\n    localparam C0 = 4'd2;\n    localparam C1 = 4'd3;\n    localparam D0 = 4'd4;\n    localparam D1 = 4'd5;\n    localparam D2 = 4'd6;\n    localparam E0 = 4'd7;\n    localparam E1 = 4'd8;\n\n    reg [3:0] state, next_state;\n\n    always @(*) begin\n        case (state)\n            A:  next_state = s ? B : A;\n\n            B:  next_state = w ? C1 : C0;\n\n            C0: next_state = w ? D1 : D0;\n            C1: next_state = w ? D2 : D1;\n\n            // Third sample: compute the final count = ones so far + w.\n            // z is 1 only when that final count equals 2.\n            D0: next_state = E0;                  // 0 + w in {0,1}  -> never 2\n            D1: next_state = w ? E1 : E0;         // 1 + w in {1,2}  -> 2 iff w=1\n            D2: next_state = w ? E0 : E1;         // 2 + w in {2,3}  -> 2 iff w=0\n\n            E0: next_state = B;\n            E1: next_state = B;\n\n            default: next_state = A;\n        endcase\n    end\n\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        if (reset)\n            state <= A;\n        else\n            state <= next_state;\n    end\n\n    assign z = (state == E1);\n\nendmodule\n"
  },
